component mag "Toolchanger magazine + shifter: fetches/returns pots, with interlocks, timeouts, fault reset and pot tracking";

description """
The shifter positions (-600 park, -757 carousel, 197 change position, 0 clear)
and clamp handshakes are unchanged from the January 2025 version.  Added:

Pot tracking - pot-out / pot-pocket say whether a pot is out of the carousel
and which pocket it belongs in.  magstate.py saves them to mag_state.txt and
hands them back at startup (saved-*), so a restart doesn't lose a pot.

Requests (iocontrol tool-prepare + tool-prep-pocket):
  - pot for that pocket already out       -> prepared straight away
  - another pot out                       -> put it back, then fetch the new one
  - pocket 0 (tool already in the spindle) -> put any pot back, prepared, no fetch
  - pocket changes while prepared (T1 then T5 before M6) -> same as above,
    no fault (acts on the pocket change itself, machine on)
  - tool-prepared is only TRUE while the out pot matches iocontrol's pocket

Interlocks (user's rules, 2026-10-14):
  - carousel only turns while the shifter is between -600 and 0
  - shifter only moves while the ATC arm is at 0 or 500 (+-arm-tol)

Faults stop everything where it is (carousel and shifter targets frozen at
their current positions, clamp outputs left as they are) and wait in state
999 with fault-step / fault-reason:
  1 step timeout
  2 shifter not clear (outside -600..0) while the carousel must turn
  3 ATC arm not at rest while the shifter must move
  4 machine turned off mid-sequence
  5 bad pocket number
  6 the out pot's position is unknown (see below) - Put pot back / pot-clear
A rising edge on fault-reset (2026-10-24) RESUMES the move that faulted
for reasons 1-4 in a fetch / return (shifter and carousel targets put back,
pot-unknown cleared - the mag has the pot again), like the atc does.  That
needs the machine on: a reset while it is off is ignored, so the move can
still be resumed afterwards.  In step mode the resumed move waits for
step-go like any other.  Other faults (5, 6, or a fault while idle /
prepared) go back to idle.  After a restart there's nothing to resume (state
starts at 0) - use Put pot back / Pot is in carousel.  Pot tracking is kept.

Pot position unknown (2026-10-24): a fault (or E-stop) mid-sequence while a
pot is out of the carousel sets pot-unknown - the pot may be anywhere
between the carousel and the change position.  While it is set, any tool
request faults with reason 6 instead of trusting the pot (it used to count
an out pot as ready, so the arm could swing with no pot at the change
position).  Clear it with return-pot (pot is at the change position) or
pot-clear (you put it back by hand).  Both work straight from a reason-6
fault too.  Saved across restarts by magstate.py.

Manual recovery (halcmd setp, later panel buttons), idle only:
  return-pot  rising edge: put the out pot back in its pocket
  pot-clear   rising edge: forget the out pot (you put it back by hand)

Shifter positions (2026-10-24): the change position (was fixed 197) and the
carousel position (was fixed -757) are pins, shifter-atc-pos and
shifter-mag-pos (from the ini), plus a trim each (shifter-atc-trim,
shifter-mag-trim, +-trim-max, from the panel).  Changing a trim while the
shifter is at / heading to that position moves it there live, as long as
the ATC arm is at rest - for setting the positions up.  Copy the result
(shifter-atc-eff / shifter-mag-eff) into the ini afterwards.

Step mode (step-mode TRUE): every shifter move, shifter clamp / unclamp and
carousel move waits for a rising edge on step-go.  While it waits
step-waiting is TRUE and next-shifter / next-pocket / next-clamp say what
the step will do (next-clamp 1 = clamp, 2 = unclamp, 0 = no change).
Timeouts don't run while waiting.

Slow mode: like the atc, speed-in / speed-full (min-speed .. 1) scales
shifter-maxv (to j7.limit3.maxv).  Shifter step timeouts count
speed-weighted time, so moving the slider mid-step doesn't trip them.

E-stop / machine off (2026-10-24): while enable is FALSE, the carousel and
shifter targets follow their real positions (car-fb, shifter-fb) and
car-hold / shifter-hold are TRUE (-> j5/j7.limit3.load), once each is
homed.  Nothing moves when the machine comes back on.  A running sequence
still faults with reason 4.
The carousel keeps its own speed.

Quick prepare ack (2026-10-24) - WORKAROUND for a LinuxCNC 2.10.0~pre1 bug:
an Abort while iocontrol's tool-prepare (or tool-change) handshake is
pending leaves task's io.status at EXEC forever (exec_state 7, MDI/program
runs hang, slow mode changes, only a restart clears it).  Fixed upstream in
commit 990cb293bd / v2.10.0-pre2.  So io-prepared (-> iocontrol.0.tool-prepared)
answers tool-prepare at once, and the request is latched here (req_pending)
and carried out as before.  tool-prepared (-> atc) still only goes TRUE when
the right pot really is at the change position, and the atc waits for it
before swapping.  Side effect: a T no longer blocks the program - the fetch
runs while the program carries on; the M6 waits for the pot.  An Abort
during an M6 can still hang task (tool-change handshake) - restart.
After upgrading LinuxCNC this can go: net iocontrol.0.tool-prepared back to
mag.0.tool-prepared in toolchanger.hal (io-prepared then unused).
""";

// --- inputs ---
pin in bit enable "machine on, motion.motion-enabled";
pin in bit magazine_ready;
pin in bit shifter_ready;
pin in signed iocontrol_prep_pocket_in "iocontrol pocket number";
pin in float j5_limit3_out "carousel position, pockets";
pin in float j7_limit3_out "shifter position";
pin in float arm_pos "ATC arm position (J6:out)";
pin in bit tool_prepare;
pin in bit shifter_clamped_sensor;
pin in bit shifter_unclamped_sensor;
pin in bit atc_changed;
pin in bit fault_reset;
pin in bit return_pot;
pin in bit pot_clear;
pin in unsigned atc_state "atc.0.state - Put pot back in prepared state only while 0 (no M6 running)";

// --- saved pot state from magstate.py ---
pin in bit saved_valid;
pin in bit saved_pot_out;
pin in signed saved_pot_pocket;
pin in bit saved_pot_unknown;

// --- outputs ---
pin out float tool_prep_pocket_out "carousel target, pockets";
pin out float shifter_pos_cmd "shifter target";
pin out bit tool_prepared;
pin out bit io_prepared "quick ack of tool-prepare -> iocontrol.0.tool-prepared (2.10 pre1 abort workaround)";
pin out bit toolchanger_faulted;
pin out bit shifter_clamp;
pin out bit shifter_unclamp;
pin out bit pot_out "a pot is out of the carousel";
pin out signed pot_pocket "pocket the out pot belongs in";
pin out bit pot_unknown "out pot position unknown (fault mid-move) - Put pot back or pot-clear";
pin out bit state_loaded "saved pot state has been read - magstate.py may save";
pin out signed fault_step;
pin out signed fault_reason;
pin out float step_time;

// --- settings ---
pin in float step_timeout = 10 "seconds for a shifter / clamp step";
pin in float carousel_timeout = 60 "seconds for a carousel move";
pin in float arm_tol = 5 "arm counts as at rest within this of 0 or 500";
pin in float shifter_tol = 0.5 "shifter clear zone is -600-tol .. 0+tol";
pin in signed pockets = 80;
pin in float shifter_atc_pos = 197 "shifter change position (arm side)";
pin in float shifter_mag_pos = -757 "shifter carousel position";
pin in float shifter_atc_trim "added to shifter-atc-pos (panel)";
pin in float shifter_mag_trim "added to shifter-mag-pos (panel)";
pin in float trim_max = 25 "trims are limited to +- this";
pin out float shifter_atc_eff "change position in use";
pin out float shifter_mag_eff "carousel position in use";

// --- step / slow mode (2026-10-24) ---
pin in bit step_mode "each shifter / clamp / carousel move waits for step-go";
pin in bit step_go "rising edge: do the next step";
pin out bit step_waiting "waiting for step-go";
pin out float next_shifter "shifter target of the waiting step";
pin out signed next_pocket "carousel pocket of the waiting step";
pin out signed next_clamp "waiting step: 1 clamp, 2 unclamp, 0 no change";
pin in float speed_in = 100 "halui.max-velocity.value (unconnected = full speed)";
pin in float speed_full = 100 "speed-in that means full speed";
pin in float min_speed = 0.02 "slowest speed fraction";
pin in float shifter_maxv_full = 240 "[JOINT_7]MAX_VELOCITY";
pin out float shifter_maxv "to j7.limit3.maxv";

// --- E-stop hold (2026-10-24) ---
pin in bit car_homed "joint.5.homed";
pin in bit shifter_homed "joint.7.homed";
pin in float car_fb "joint.5.pos-fb";
pin in float shifter_fb "joint.7.pos-fb";
pin out bit car_hold "machine off: to j5.limit3.load";
pin out bit shifter_hold "machine off: to j7.limit3.load";

// Debugging
pin io unsigned state;
pin out bit default_bit;

variable int prepared_pocket;
variable int want_pocket;
variable int fetch_after;
variable int car_sent;
variable int prev_atc_changed;
variable int prev_fault_reset;
variable int prev_return_pot;
variable int prev_tool_prepare;
variable int req_pending;
variable int prev_pot_clear;
variable unsigned prev_state;
variable int prev_step_go;
variable int go_armed;
variable double work_time;
variable float prev_atc_eff = 197;
variable float prev_mag_eff = -757;
variable float saved_shifter;
variable float saved_pocket;
variable int resume_pending;

function _;

license "GPL";
author "Andrew Beck, Luke Beck; interlocks, timeouts, pot tracking added 2026-10-14; step / slow mode, shifter trims, E-stop hold, pot-unknown, reset-resume 2026-10-24";
include <stdlib.h>;
;;

#include <rtapi_math.h>

/* states - fetch keeps the original numbers, return keeps 80-130 */
#define ST_IDLE        0
#define ST_FETCH_GO    5    /* carousel to pocket, shifter to -600 */
#define ST_FETCH_IN   10    /* shifter in to the carousel (MAG_POS) */
#define ST_FETCH_GRAB 20    /* clamp */
#define ST_FETCH_OUT  30    /* shifter out to the change position (ATC_POS) */
#define ST_FETCH_LET  40    /* unclamp */
#define ST_FETCH_BACK 50    /* shifter back to 0 */
#define ST_FETCH_DONE 60
#define ST_PREPARED   70
#define ST_RET_GO     75    /* carousel to the out pot's pocket */
#define ST_RET_UNCL   80    /* unclamp, then shifter to ATC_POS */
#define ST_RET_GRAB   90    /* clamp */
#define ST_RET_IN    100    /* shifter in to MAG_POS */
#define ST_RET_LET   110    /* unclamp */
#define ST_RET_PARK  120    /* shifter to -600 */
#define ST_RET_DONE  130
#define ST_FAULT     999

#define R_TIMEOUT     1
#define R_SHIFTER     2
#define R_ARM         3
#define R_MACHINE     4
#define R_POCKET      5
#define R_POT_UNKNOWN 6

/* shifter positions in use (pins + trims, see FUNCTION) */
#define ATC_POS shifter_atc_eff
#define MAG_POS shifter_mag_eff

#define NEAR(a, b) (fabs((a) - (b)) < 0.01)
#define SHIFTER_AT(p) NEAR(j7_limit3_out, (p))
#define CAROUSEL_AT_TARGET NEAR(j5_limit3_out, tool_prep_pocket_out)
#define UNCLAMPED (shifter_unclamped_sensor && !shifter_clamped_sensor)
#define CLAMPED   (shifter_clamped_sensor && !shifter_unclamped_sensor)

#define TRIP(reason) do { \
    toolchanger_faulted = 1; \
    saved_shifter = shifter_pos_cmd; \
    saved_pocket = tool_prep_pocket_out; \
    if (pot_out && state != ST_IDLE && state != ST_PREPARED) pot_unknown = 1; \
    fault_step = state; \
    fault_reason = (reason); \
    tool_prep_pocket_out = j5_limit3_out; \
    shifter_pos_cmd = j7_limit3_out; \
    tool_prepared = 0; \
    state = ST_FAULT; \
} while (0)

static int modulo(int value, int range) {
    int r = value % range;
    return r < 0 ? r + range : r;
}

/* carousel position (unbounded, in pockets) for pocket `finish`, going the
   short way round from `start` */
static int shortest_path(int start, int finish, int n) {
    int dis_clock = modulo(finish - start, n);
    int dis_anti = n - dis_clock;
    return dis_anti < dis_clock ? start - dis_anti : start + dis_clock;
}

FUNCTION(_) {
    int arm_rest = fabs(arm_pos) <= arm_tol || fabs(arm_pos - 500) <= arm_tol;
    int shifter_clear = j7_limit3_out >= -600 - shifter_tol && j7_limit3_out <= shifter_tol;
    int carousel_pocket = modulo((int)floor(j5_limit3_out + 0.5), pockets);
    int atc_done = atc_changed && !prev_atc_changed;
    int reset = fault_reset && !prev_fault_reset;
    int ret_req = return_pot && !prev_return_pot;
    int clr_req = pot_clear && !prev_pot_clear;
    int moving_carousel, moving_shifter;
    double speed = speed_full > 0 ? speed_in / speed_full : 1;
    double atc_trim = shifter_atc_trim, mag_trim = shifter_mag_trim;
    unsigned snap_state;
    float snap_shifter, snap_pocket;
    int snap_clamp, snap_unclamp, snap_prepared, snap_pot_out, snap_pot_pocket;
    int snap_want, snap_prepared_pocket, snap_fetch_after, snap_car_sent, snap_req;

    /* slow mode - shifter only, the carousel keeps its speed */
    if (speed > 1) speed = 1;
    if (speed < min_speed) speed = min_speed;
    if (speed <= 0) speed = 1;
    shifter_maxv = shifter_maxv_full * speed;

    /* shifter positions + trims; a trim change moves the shifter live if
       it is at / heading to that position and the arm is at rest */
    if (atc_trim > trim_max) atc_trim = trim_max;
    if (atc_trim < -trim_max) atc_trim = -trim_max;
    if (mag_trim > trim_max) mag_trim = trim_max;
    if (mag_trim < -trim_max) mag_trim = -trim_max;
    shifter_atc_eff = shifter_atc_pos + atc_trim;
    shifter_mag_eff = shifter_mag_pos + mag_trim;
    if (state != ST_FAULT && arm_rest) {
        if (NEAR(shifter_pos_cmd, prev_atc_eff)) shifter_pos_cmd = shifter_atc_eff;
        else if (NEAR(shifter_pos_cmd, prev_mag_eff)) shifter_pos_cmd = shifter_mag_eff;
        prev_atc_eff = shifter_atc_eff;
        prev_mag_eff = shifter_mag_eff;
    }

    /* step mode: Next only counts while a step is waiting */
    if (!step_mode) go_armed = 0;
    else if (step_go && !prev_step_go && step_waiting) go_armed = 1;
    prev_step_go = step_go;
    step_waiting = 0;

    prev_atc_changed = atc_changed;
    prev_fault_reset = fault_reset;
    prev_return_pot = return_pot;

    /* latch the tool request - iocontrol only holds tool-prepare until
       io-prepared answers it */
    if (tool_prepare && !prev_tool_prepare) req_pending = 1;
    prev_tool_prepare = tool_prepare;
    io_prepared = tool_prepare && state_loaded;
    prev_pot_clear = pot_clear;

    /* load the saved pot state once */
    if (!state_loaded) {
        if (!saved_valid) return;
        pot_out = saved_pot_out;
        pot_pocket = saved_pot_pocket;
        pot_unknown = saved_pot_out && saved_pot_unknown;
        tool_prep_pocket_out = j5_limit3_out;
        shifter_pos_cmd = j7_limit3_out;
        state_loaded = 1;
    }

    /* step timer */
    if (state != prev_state) { step_time = 0; work_time = 0; }
    else { step_time += fperiod; work_time += fperiod * speed; }
    prev_state = state;

    /* Put pot back / pot-clear also clear a "pot position unknown" fault */
    if (state == ST_FAULT && fault_reason == R_POT_UNKNOWN && (clr_req || ret_req)) {
        toolchanger_faulted = 0;
        fault_step = 0;
        fault_reason = 0;
        state = ST_IDLE;
    }

    if (reset && state == ST_FAULT) {
        int resumable = fault_reason >= R_TIMEOUT && fault_reason <= R_MACHINE
                        && fault_step != ST_IDLE && fault_step != ST_PREPARED;
        if (resumable && !enable) {
            /* machine off: keep the fault, the move can be resumed later */
        } else {
            if (resumable) {
                /* carry on with the move that faulted; targets go back
                   below, after the step-mode snapshot */
                state = fault_step;
                resume_pending = 1;
                /* fresh timer: the time spent faulted doesn't count */
                prev_state = ~0u;
                step_time = 0;
                work_time = 0;
                pot_unknown = 0;
            } else {
                state = ST_IDLE;
            }
            toolchanger_faulted = 0;
            fault_step = 0;
            fault_reason = 0;
        }
    }

    /* checks while a sequence is running */
    if (state != ST_IDLE && state != ST_PREPARED && state != ST_FAULT) {
        moving_carousel = !CAROUSEL_AT_TARGET;
        moving_shifter = !NEAR(j7_limit3_out, shifter_pos_cmd);
        if (!enable)                                TRIP(R_MACHINE);
        else if (moving_carousel && !shifter_clear) TRIP(R_SHIFTER);
        else if (moving_shifter && !arm_rest)       TRIP(R_ARM);
        else if ((state == ST_FETCH_GO || state == ST_RET_GO)
                 ? step_time > carousel_timeout : work_time > step_timeout)
                                                    TRIP(R_TIMEOUT);
    }

    /* snapshot for step mode */
    snap_state = state;
    snap_shifter = shifter_pos_cmd;
    snap_pocket = tool_prep_pocket_out;
    snap_clamp = shifter_clamp;
    snap_unclamp = shifter_unclamp;
    snap_prepared = tool_prepared;
    snap_pot_out = pot_out;
    snap_pot_pocket = pot_pocket;
    snap_want = want_pocket;
    snap_prepared_pocket = prepared_pocket;
    snap_fetch_after = fetch_after;
    snap_car_sent = car_sent;
    snap_req = req_pending;

    /* resume after a fault reset: put the targets back (held back by step
       mode like any other move) */
    if (resume_pending) {
        shifter_pos_cmd = saved_shifter;
        tool_prep_pocket_out = saved_pocket;
    }

    switch (state) {
    case ST_IDLE:
        tool_prepared = 0;
        if (clr_req) { pot_out = 0; pot_unknown = 0; }
        if (ret_req && pot_out) {
            pot_unknown = 0;             /* user says it is at the change position */
            fetch_after = 0;
            want_pocket = 0;
            state = ST_RET_GO;
            break;
        }
        if (!req_pending || !enable) break;
        req_pending = 0;
        if (pot_out && pot_unknown) { TRIP(R_POT_UNKNOWN); break; }
        want_pocket = iocontrol_prep_pocket_in;
        if (want_pocket < 0 || want_pocket > pockets) { TRIP(R_POCKET); break; }
        if (want_pocket == 0) {
            /* tool already in the spindle - nothing to fetch */
            if (pot_out) { fetch_after = 0; req_pending = 1; state = ST_RET_GO; }  /* still asked: prepared after */
            else { prepared_pocket = 0; tool_prepared = 1; state = ST_PREPARED; }
        } else if (pot_out && pot_pocket == want_pocket) {
            prepared_pocket = want_pocket; tool_prepared = 1; state = ST_PREPARED;
        } else if (pot_out) {
            fetch_after = 1; state = ST_RET_GO;
        } else {
            state = ST_FETCH_GO;
        }
        break;

    /* ---------------- fetch a pot ---------------- */
    case ST_FETCH_GO:
        /* unclamp, park the shifter at -600 (it may have been left at MAG_POS
           by a fault), and only then turn the carousel */
        if (step_time == 0) {
            if (!arm_rest) { TRIP(R_ARM); break; }
            shifter_clamp = 0;
            shifter_unclamp = 1;
            car_sent = 0;
        }
        if (UNCLAMPED && !NEAR(shifter_pos_cmd, -600)) shifter_pos_cmd = -600;
        if (SHIFTER_AT(-600) && !car_sent) {
            int dest = shortest_path((int)floor(j5_limit3_out + 0.5), want_pocket, pockets);
            if (abs(dest) >= 80000000) { TRIP(R_POCKET); break; }
            tool_prep_pocket_out = dest;
            car_sent = 1;
        }
        if (CAROUSEL_AT_TARGET && carousel_pocket == modulo(want_pocket, pockets)
                && SHIFTER_AT(-600) && UNCLAMPED) {
            shifter_pos_cmd = MAG_POS;
            state = ST_FETCH_IN;
        }
        break;

    case ST_FETCH_IN:
        if (SHIFTER_AT(MAG_POS)) {
            shifter_unclamp = 0;
            shifter_clamp = 1;
            state = ST_FETCH_GRAB;
        }
        break;

    case ST_FETCH_GRAB:
        if (CLAMPED) {
            shifter_pos_cmd = ATC_POS;
            pot_out = 1;                 /* pot is leaving the carousel */
            pot_pocket = want_pocket;
            state = ST_FETCH_OUT;
        }
        break;

    case ST_FETCH_OUT:
        if (SHIFTER_AT(ATC_POS)) {
            shifter_clamp = 0;
            shifter_unclamp = 1;
            state = ST_FETCH_LET;
        }
        break;

    case ST_FETCH_LET:
        if (UNCLAMPED) {
            shifter_pos_cmd = 0;
            state = ST_FETCH_BACK;
        }
        break;

    case ST_FETCH_BACK:
        if (SHIFTER_AT(0)) state = ST_FETCH_DONE;
        break;

    case ST_FETCH_DONE:
        prepared_pocket = want_pocket;
        tool_prepared = 1;
        state = ST_PREPARED;
        break;

    /* ---------------- prepared, waiting for M6 ---------------- */
    case ST_PREPARED:
        if (ret_req && pot_out && atc_state == 0 && arm_rest) {
            /* Put pot back after an aborted program (2026-10-24): the pot
               goes home, iocontrol keeps its stale prepare, so an M6 now
               stops at atc "not prepared" until a new T is given */
            tool_prepared = 0;
            fetch_after = 0;
            want_pocket = 0;
            state = ST_RET_GO;
        } else if (atc_done) {
            /* the pot now holds the old tool - it goes back to the same pocket */
            tool_prepared = 0;
            fetch_after = 0;
            state = ST_RET_GO;
        } else if (enable && iocontrol_prep_pocket_in != prepared_pocket) {
            /* new T before M6: swap pots, no fault.  Don't wait for the
               tool-prepare pulse - iocontrol sees tool-prepared still TRUE
               from the last T and drops tool-prepare before we notice. */
            tool_prepared = 0;
            want_pocket = iocontrol_prep_pocket_in;
            if (want_pocket < 0 || want_pocket > pockets) { TRIP(R_POCKET); break; }
            if (!pot_out) {
                state = want_pocket == 0 ? ST_IDLE : ST_FETCH_GO;
            } else if (want_pocket == pot_pocket) {
                prepared_pocket = want_pocket; tool_prepared = 1;
            } else {
                fetch_after = want_pocket != 0;
                state = ST_RET_GO;
            }
        }
        break;

    /* ---------------- return the out pot ---------------- */
    case ST_RET_GO:
        if (step_time == 0) {
            int dest = shortest_path((int)floor(j5_limit3_out + 0.5), pot_pocket, pockets);
            if (abs(dest) >= 80000000) { TRIP(R_POCKET); break; }
            if (!shifter_clear) { TRIP(R_SHIFTER); break; }
            tool_prep_pocket_out = dest;
        }
        if (CAROUSEL_AT_TARGET && carousel_pocket == modulo(pot_pocket, pockets)) {
            if (!arm_rest) { TRIP(R_ARM); break; }
            shifter_clamp = 0;
            shifter_unclamp = 1;
            state = ST_RET_UNCL;
        }
        break;

    case ST_RET_UNCL:
        if (UNCLAMPED && !NEAR(shifter_pos_cmd, ATC_POS)) shifter_pos_cmd = ATC_POS;
        if (SHIFTER_AT(ATC_POS)) {
            shifter_unclamp = 0;
            shifter_clamp = 1;
            state = ST_RET_GRAB;
        }
        break;

    case ST_RET_GRAB:
        if (CLAMPED) {
            shifter_pos_cmd = MAG_POS;
            state = ST_RET_IN;
        }
        break;

    case ST_RET_IN:
        if (SHIFTER_AT(MAG_POS)) {
            shifter_clamp = 0;
            shifter_unclamp = 1;
            state = ST_RET_LET;
        }
        break;

    case ST_RET_LET:
        if (UNCLAMPED) {
            pot_out = 0;                 /* pot is back in its pocket */
            shifter_pos_cmd = -600;
            state = ST_RET_PARK;
        }
        break;

    case ST_RET_PARK:
        if (SHIFTER_AT(-600)) state = ST_RET_DONE;
        break;

    case ST_RET_DONE:
        if (fetch_after) {
            fetch_after = 0;
            state = ST_FETCH_GO;
        } else if (req_pending && want_pocket == 0) {
            req_pending = 0;
            prepared_pocket = 0;
            tool_prepared = 1;
            state = ST_PREPARED;
        } else {
            state = ST_IDLE;
        }
        break;

    case ST_FAULT:
        break;

    default:
        default_bit = 1;
        break;
    }

    /* never claim prepared for a pocket iocontrol isn't asking for */
    if (state != ST_PREPARED || iocontrol_prep_pocket_in != prepared_pocket)
        tool_prepared = 0;

    /* step mode: a step that moves the shifter or carousel or changes the
       shifter clamp is held back (everything put back as it was) until
       Next is pressed */
    if (step_mode && state != ST_FAULT
            && (shifter_pos_cmd != snap_shifter || tool_prep_pocket_out != snap_pocket
                || shifter_clamp != snap_clamp || shifter_unclamp != snap_unclamp)) {
        if (go_armed) {
            go_armed = 0;
        } else {
            next_shifter = shifter_pos_cmd;
            next_pocket = modulo((int)floor(tool_prep_pocket_out + 0.5), pockets);
            next_clamp = shifter_clamp != snap_clamp || shifter_unclamp != snap_unclamp
                         ? (shifter_clamp ? 1 : 2) : 0;
            state = snap_state;
            shifter_pos_cmd = snap_shifter;
            tool_prep_pocket_out = snap_pocket;
            shifter_clamp = snap_clamp;
            shifter_unclamp = snap_unclamp;
            tool_prepared = snap_prepared;
            pot_out = snap_pot_out;
            pot_pocket = snap_pot_pocket;
            want_pocket = snap_want;
            prepared_pocket = snap_prepared_pocket;
            fetch_after = snap_fetch_after;
            car_sent = snap_car_sent;
            req_pending = snap_req;
            step_waiting = 1;
            /* re-enter the state next cycle: timer from 0, one-shots run again */
            prev_state = ~0u;
            step_time = 0;
            work_time = 0;
        }
    }

    if (resume_pending && !step_waiting) resume_pending = 0;

    /* a request made while fetching / prepared is followed by the pocket
       number (FETCH_DONE -> PREPARED compares it); a faulted mag drops it
       (the fault aborts the program) */
    if ((state >= ST_FETCH_GO && state <= ST_PREPARED) || state == ST_FAULT) req_pending = 0;

    /* E-stop / machine off: targets = where things really are */
    car_hold = !enable && car_homed;
    shifter_hold = !enable && shifter_homed;
    if (car_hold) tool_prep_pocket_out = car_fb;
    if (shifter_hold) shifter_pos_cmd = shifter_fb;
}
